                    status: Completed,
                    detail: Think {
                        output: Some(
                            "Here is the complete map.\n\n## 1. Channel message structs (Rust)\n\n**Domain (canonical) — `crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs`**\n\n- `ChannelMessage` (top-level timeline message) — **line 140**\n```rust\n/// A top-level message with thread info, reactions, and attachments.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct ChannelMessage {\n    pub id: Uuid,\n    pub channel_id: Uuid,\n    pub sender_id: String,\n    /// For an agent (bot) message, the id of the user who triggered it.\n    pub triggered_by: Option<String>,\n    /// Bot profile when the sender is a bot.\n    pub bot_profile: Option<BotSenderProfile>,\n    pub content: String,\n    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n    pub edited_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,\n    pub deleted_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,\n    pub thread: ThreadInfo,\n    pub reactions: Vec<CountedReaction>,\n    pub attachments: Vec<MessageAttachment>,\n}\n```\n- `ThreadInfo` (line 200), `ThreadReply` (line 212 — same shape, no `thread`/`deleted_at`), `CountedReaction` (line 240), `MessageAttachment` (line 249)\n- `ChannelContextMessage` (line 366) — flat shape used by the message-context endpoint (has `thread_id`)\n- `RecentChannelMessage` (line 175) — lightweight shape used for AI attachments / search indexing, adds `mentions: Vec<String>` formatted `{ENTITY_TYPE}:{ENTITY_ID}`\n- `MutatedMessage` (line 1028) — what mutations return / what gets broadcast over realtime; `sender_id: ChannelSender<'static>`\n- Raw DB row types: `TopLevelMessageRow` (line 431), `ThreadReplyRow` (line 465), `ThreadData` (line 452)\n- Requests: `PostMessageRequest` (line 913 — `content: String`, `mentions: Vec<SimpleMention>`, `thread_id`, `attachments`, `nonce`, internal-only `triggered_by`), `PatchMessageRequest` (line 946), `PostMessageResponse` (line 939)\n- `SimpleMention` (line 797) = `{ entity_type: String, entity_id: String }`\n\n**DB row / SQL** — `crates/channels/src/outbound/pg_channels_repo.rs` (row structs at lines 72–290: `TopLevelRow`, `ThreadDataRow`, `ContextMessageRow` at 165, `MutatedMessageRow` at 209).\nTable DDL: `crates/macro_db_client/migrations/20251104101012_comms_db_schema.sql:93`\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE public.comms_messages\n(\n    id uuid NOT NULL, channel_id uuid NOT NULL, thread_id uuid,\n    sender_id text NOT NULL, content text NOT NULL,\n    created_at timestamptz NOT NULL, updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    edited_at timestamp, deleted_at timestamp\n);\n```\nplus `crates/macro_db_client/migrations/20260629171949_add_comms_messages_triggered_by.sql:11` → `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS triggered_by_user_id text;`\nContent is a single `text` column. There is **no** content-type/kind column, no jsonb.\n\n**API/response types — `crates/channels/src/inbound/axum_router.rs`** (mounted by `services/document_storage_service/src/main.rs:1072`)\n- `ApiChannelMessage` — **line 1911**, `ApiChannelMessagesPage` — 1817, `ApiThreadInfo` — 2107, `ApiThreadReply` — 2137, `ApiChannelContextMessage` — 1978, `ApiMessageSender` — 1829, `ApiMessageSenderType` — 1849\n```rust\npub struct ApiChannelMessage {\n    id: Uuid, channel_id: Uuid,\n    sender_id: String,\n    sender: ApiMessageSender,\n    content: String,\n    created_at/updated_at/edited_at/deleted_at,\n    thread: ApiThreadInfo,\n    reactions: Vec<ApiCountedReaction>,\n    attachments: Vec<ApiMessageAttachment>,\n}\n```\n\n**Other parallel copies of the same shape:**\n- Soup/inbox: `crates/models_soup/src/comms.rs:78` `ChannelMessage`, `:120` `SoupChannelThread`, `:155` `SoupMessageSender`, `:167` `SoupMessageSenderType`\n- MCP toolset: `crates/channels/src/inbound/toolset/types.rs` (`ToolMessageKind` at 33, message types ~263)\n- Search indexing: `crates/comms_db_client/src/messages/get_channel_message.rs:6` `ChannelMessageInfo`; `crates/models_search/src/channel.rs:129`; `crates/opensearch_client/src/search/channels.rs:23`\n- Realtime websocket payload: `crates/channels/src/outbound/connection_gateway_realtime.rs:159` `MessageRealtimeData` (flattens `MutatedMessage` + `MessageRealtimeSender` at 166)\n\n## 2. How content is represented\n\n**Plain `String`.** Markdown text, rendered client-side. No content blocks, no enum of part types, no structured/rich parts anywhere in the channel path — every layer (`ChannelMessage`, `ThreadReply`, `ApiChannelMessage`, `MutatedMessage`, `TopLevelMessageRow`, soup, search, DB column) carries `content: String`.\n\nThe only structure adjacent to content:\n- Inline mention markup embedded *inside* the markdown string, extracted by the lexical service into `SimpleMention` rows (`crates/lexical_mention_extractor/src/lib.rs:27`, table `comms_entity_mentions`).\n- `MessageAttachment` / `comms_attachments` as a sibling list (entity_type/entity_id + width/height), not part of content.\n\nFrontend rendering: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/Content.tsx:14` — takes `message().content` and passes it whole to `StaticMarkdown` with `channelTheme`. `isEmojiOnly` bumps to big-emoji styling. That's the entire content rendering model.\n\n## 3. Non-human / bot / AI author — yes, this exists\n\n- `crates/channel_sender/src/lib.rs:18` — `ChannelSender<'a>(Either<BotIdStr, MacroUserIdStr>)`; `sender_id` in the DB is a namespaced principal string, parsed via `parse_from_str` (tries `BotIdStr` first, i.e. `bot|<uuid>`, else macro user id).\n- `crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs:25` — `BotSenderProfile { name: String, avatar_url: Option<String> }`\n- API discriminator: `crates/channels/src/inbound/axum_router.rs:1829-1853`\n```rust\npub struct ApiMessageSender {\n    #[serde(rename = \"type\")] sender_type: ApiMessageSenderType,\n    id: String,                      // bot uuid or user id, namespace stripped\n    name: Option<String>,            // bot display name\n    avatar_url: Option<String>,      // bot avatar\n    triggered_by: Option<String>,    // user who triggered the agent message\n}\npub enum ApiMessageSenderType { User, Bot }   // snake_case on the wire\n```\nbuilt by `ApiMessageSender::from_message_sender` (line 1893) — bot profile + `triggered_by` only attached when the sender is a bot.\n- `triggered_by` is set internally, never from the wire (`PostMessageRequest.triggered_by`, `#[serde(skip)]`).\n- Bot model: `crates/bots/src/domain/models.rs:104` `Bot { id: BotId, kind: BotKind, owner: Option<BotOwner>, name, handle, description, avatar_url, ... }`; `BotKind { Owned, System }` at line 14; `BotOwner { User{user_id}, Team{team_id} }` at line 87. Related crates: `crates/bot_id`, `crates/channel_bots`.\n- Frontend: `apps/web/src/lib/queries/channel/message-sender.ts` (`isBotSenderId`, `senderFromStorageId`, `normalizeChannelMessageSender`), `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/AgentBadge.tsx` (renders an \"Agent\" pill when `isBotSenderId(sender_id)`), `apps/web/src/features/channel/macroAi.ts` + `@core/constant/macroAgent` (the first-party Macro agent bot identity, `MACRO_AGENT_PRINCIPAL_ID` = `bot|<uuid>`).\n\n## 4. Message \"kind\"/\"type\" discriminator — none for content\n\nThe only `kind` that exists is **position**, not content type: `ChannelMessageKind { TopLevelMessage, ThreadReply }` at `crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs:104`, surfaced as `ApiChannelMessageKind` (`axum_router.rs:2198`) and `ToolMessageKind` (`toolset/types.rs:33`).\n\nThere is **no** system-message / join-leave / call-event variant on `comms_messages`. Non-plain-text UI is modeled *outside* the message stream:\n- Active call banner: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Channel/ActiveCallMessage.tsx` — a separate component driven by `useActiveCallQuery`, not a message row.\n- Channel-created marker: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/ChannelCreatedIndicator.tsx` — list decoration.\n- Date/new dividers: `DateDivider.tsx`, `NewDivider.tsx` — list decorations keyed off `ChannelMessageListMeta` (`Message/list-meta.ts`).\n- Deleted state: branch on `message.deleted_at != null` (`ChannelMessage.tsx:227` → `DeletedMessageLayout`).\n- Call transcripts fake a message: `apps/web/src/features/block-call/component/CallTranscript.tsx:79` `segmentToApiChannelMessage(...)` synthesizes an `ApiChannelMessage` from a transcript segment. Same trick for doc comments: `apps/web/src/lib/core/comments/discussion/Discussion.tsx:182` `discussionCommentToApiChannelMessage`.\n\nSo today the only way to render anything non-plain-text is to either synthesize a fake `ApiChannelMessage` or add a sibling component to the list.\n\n## 5. TypeScript types + renderer\n\n**Not specta.** utoipa → OpenAPI JSON → **orval** codegen.\n- Config: `apps/web/src/lib/service-clients/orval.config.ts` (channels live in the `document_storage_service` spec → `service-storage`).\n- Generated: `apps/web/src/lib/service-clients/service-storage/generated/schemas/apiChannelMessage.ts`, `apiMessageSender.ts`, `apiMessageSenderType.ts` (`{ user: 'user', bot: 'bot' }`), `apiThreadInfo.ts`, `apiThreadReply.ts`, `apiCountedReaction.ts`, `apiMessageAttachment.ts`, `apiChannelMessagesPage.ts`, `apiChannelMessageKind.ts`, plus `soupMessageSender*.ts`. Imported as `@service-storage/generated/schemas/...` or `@service-storage/client` (tsconfig path at `apps/web/tsconfig.json:92`).\n\n**Renderer:**\n- `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/ChannelMessage.tsx:198` — `ChannelMessage()`, the row component (Switch over deleted / grouped / regular layouts).\n- Compound namespace: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/Message.ts` — `Message.{Root, Layout, Slot, SenderName, AgentBadge, FromPill, SenderIcon, Timestamp, Content, Attachments, Reactions, EditedIndicator, HoverActions, ActionMenu, MediaPreview, ...}`\n- Frontend view model (deliberately looser than the API type): `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/types.ts` — `MessageData { id, content, sender_id, sender?: ApiMessageSender, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at?, edited_at?, thread_id?, attachments, reactions }`. This is what the whole Message tree consumes via `useMessage()` (`Message/context.ts`).\n- Consumers: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Thread/ChannelThread.tsx:308`, `Thread/ThreadReplyList.tsx:85`, `Channel/ThreadList.tsx` (virtua virtualizer), `apps/web/src/features/entity/composed/list-entity/channel.tsx:171`.\n- Queries/cache: `apps/web/src/lib/queries/channel/channel-messages.ts`, `reconcile.ts`, `message-sender.ts`.\n\n## 6. AI chat message model (for comparison)\n\n**Content parts enum — `crates/agent/src/types.rs`**\n- `Role` — line 32: `{ User, Assistant, System }` (lowercase)\n- `AssistantMessagePart` — **line 52**, `#[serde(tag = \"type\", rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`:\n```rust\npub enum AssistantMessagePart {\n    Text { text: String },\n    ToolCall { name: String, json: serde_json::Value, id: String },\n    McpToolCall { name: String, service: String, display_name: Option<String>, json: serde_json::Value, id: String },\n    ToolCallResponseJson { name: String, json: serde_json::Value, id: String },\n    ToolCallErr { name: String, description: String, id: String },\n    Thinking { thinking: String },\n}\n```\n- `ChatMessageContent` — **line 136**:\n```rust\n#[serde(untagged)]\npub enum ChatMessageContent {\n    Text(String),\n    AssistantMessageParts(Vec<AssistantMessagePart>),\n}\n```\nwith helpers `user_message_text`, `assistant_message_text`, `assistant_message_text_with_tools`, `message_text`, `message_text_with_tools` (lines 148–232). `ChatMessage { content, role, attachments }` at line 240; `ChatMessages(Vec<ChatMessage>)` at 255.\n\n**Persisted / API types — `crates/model/src/chat/message.rs`**\n- `ChatMessage` (line 10): `{ id: String, content: ChatMessageContent, role: Role, model: Option<String> }`, `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`, `sqlx::FromRow`\n- `ChatMessageWithAttachments` (line 23): same + `attachments: Vec<Entity<'static>>`\n- `NewChatMessage` (line 35)\n- DB: `public.\"ChatMessage\"` with **`content jsonb NOT NULL`** and `role text` — see `services/delete_chat_handler/migrations/20240325143515_basic_schema_for_testing.sql:343`\n- Chat crate: `crates/chat/src/domain/models/chat.rs:83` `ChatResponse { messages: Vec<ChatMessageWithAttachments>, ... }`; `crates/chat/src/domain/models/message.rs:8` `PatchChatMessageArgs { message_id, content: ChatMessageContent }`, `WebCitation` (line 17), `ResolvedMessageContent` (line 34); `crates/chat/src/domain/events.rs:104` `ChatMessageRole`.\n\n**Frontend AI renderer** (the analogue of `Message/Content.tsx`): `apps/web/src/lib/core/component/AI/component/message/AssistantMessageParts.tsx` — switches on `part.type` (`toolCall` / `mcpToolCall` / `toolCallErr` / `thinking` / `text`) into `RenderTool`, `McpToolCall`, `ThinkingBlock`, `ChatMessageMarkdown`, grouping tool activity into `AssistantActivityGroup`. Types come from `@service-cognition/generated/schemas/assistantMessagePart` (orval, cognition service spec).\n\n**Key contrast:** AI chat already has a tagged, extensible part enum persisted as jsonb with a per-part-type frontend renderer registry; channel messages are a flat `text` column with a single markdown renderer, and the only author/kind discriminators are `ApiMessageSenderType { user, bot }` (author) and `ChannelMessageKind { TopLevelMessage, ThreadReply }` (position). There is no content-kind discriminator on channel messages at all.",
                        ),
                    },
                    raw_input: Some(
                        Object {
                            "subagent_type": String("Explore"),
                            "description": String("Find comms message models"),
                            "run_in_background": Bool(false),
                            "prompt": String("In /Users/eric/Code/macro, find the canonical Rust models for **channel messages** (comms messages) — the type that gets rendered in a channel in the frontend, plus its content/body representation.\n\nBe very thorough. I need to know:\n1. Where the channel message struct(s) live (crate + file paths + line numbers) — both the DB row type and the API/response type if they differ.\n2. How message *content* is represented — plain text? rich content blocks? an enum of block types? Is there any existing notion of structured/rich content parts?\n3. Whether there's any existing notion of a non-human / bot / AI author on a channel message (author type enum, bot user, sender kind, etc.).\n4. Any existing message \"kind\"/\"type\" discriminator on channel messages (e.g. system messages, join/leave, call events) — how are non-plain-text messages modeled today?\n5. Where the TypeScript types for these come from (specta export? generated swagger types?) and the frontend component that renders a channel message.\n6. Also check for the `chat` crate's AI message model (assistant messages, tool calls, content blocks) since AI chat messages already exist somewhere in this repo — I want to compare how AI content is modeled there vs channel messages.\n\nReport concrete file:line references and paste the key struct/enum definitions verbatim. Do not modify any files."),
                        },
                    ),
                    raw_output: Some(
                        Array [
                            Object {
                                "type": String("text"),
                                "text": String("Here is the complete map.\n\n## 1. Channel message structs (Rust)\n\n**Domain (canonical) — `crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs`**\n\n- `ChannelMessage` (top-level timeline message) — **line 140**\n```rust\n/// A top-level message with thread info, reactions, and attachments.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct ChannelMessage {\n    pub id: Uuid,\n    pub channel_id: Uuid,\n    pub sender_id: String,\n    /// For an agent (bot) message, the id of the user who triggered it.\n    pub triggered_by: Option<String>,\n    /// Bot profile when the sender is a bot.\n    pub bot_profile: Option<BotSenderProfile>,\n    pub content: String,\n    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n    pub edited_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,\n    pub deleted_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,\n    pub thread: ThreadInfo,\n    pub reactions: Vec<CountedReaction>,\n    pub attachments: Vec<MessageAttachment>,\n}\n```\n- `ThreadInfo` (line 200), `ThreadReply` (line 212 — same shape, no `thread`/`deleted_at`), `CountedReaction` (line 240), `MessageAttachment` (line 249)\n- `ChannelContextMessage` (line 366) — flat shape used by the message-context endpoint (has `thread_id`)\n- `RecentChannelMessage` (line 175) — lightweight shape used for AI attachments / search indexing, adds `mentions: Vec<String>` formatted `{ENTITY_TYPE}:{ENTITY_ID}`\n- `MutatedMessage` (line 1028) — what mutations return / what gets broadcast over realtime; `sender_id: ChannelSender<'static>`\n- Raw DB row types: `TopLevelMessageRow` (line 431), `ThreadReplyRow` (line 465), `ThreadData` (line 452)\n- Requests: `PostMessageRequest` (line 913 — `content: String`, `mentions: Vec<SimpleMention>`, `thread_id`, `attachments`, `nonce`, internal-only `triggered_by`), `PatchMessageRequest` (line 946), `PostMessageResponse` (line 939)\n- `SimpleMention` (line 797) = `{ entity_type: String, entity_id: String }`\n\n**DB row / SQL** — `crates/channels/src/outbound/pg_channels_repo.rs` (row structs at lines 72–290: `TopLevelRow`, `ThreadDataRow`, `ContextMessageRow` at 165, `MutatedMessageRow` at 209).\nTable DDL: `crates/macro_db_client/migrations/20251104101012_comms_db_schema.sql:93`\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE public.comms_messages\n(\n    id uuid NOT NULL, channel_id uuid NOT NULL, thread_id uuid,\n    sender_id text NOT NULL, content text NOT NULL,\n    created_at timestamptz NOT NULL, updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    edited_at timestamp, deleted_at timestamp\n);\n```\nplus `crates/macro_db_client/migrations/20260629171949_add_comms_messages_triggered_by.sql:11` → `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS triggered_by_user_id text;`\nContent is a single `text` column. There is **no** content-type/kind column, no jsonb.\n\n**API/response types — `crates/channels/src/inbound/axum_router.rs`** (mounted by `services/document_storage_service/src/main.rs:1072`)\n- `ApiChannelMessage` — **line 1911**, `ApiChannelMessagesPage` — 1817, `ApiThreadInfo` — 2107, `ApiThreadReply` — 2137, `ApiChannelContextMessage` — 1978, `ApiMessageSender` — 1829, `ApiMessageSenderType` — 1849\n```rust\npub struct ApiChannelMessage {\n    id: Uuid, channel_id: Uuid,\n    sender_id: String,\n    sender: ApiMessageSender,\n    content: String,\n    created_at/updated_at/edited_at/deleted_at,\n    thread: ApiThreadInfo,\n    reactions: Vec<ApiCountedReaction>,\n    attachments: Vec<ApiMessageAttachment>,\n}\n```\n\n**Other parallel copies of the same shape:**\n- Soup/inbox: `crates/models_soup/src/comms.rs:78` `ChannelMessage`, `:120` `SoupChannelThread`, `:155` `SoupMessageSender`, `:167` `SoupMessageSenderType`\n- MCP toolset: `crates/channels/src/inbound/toolset/types.rs` (`ToolMessageKind` at 33, message types ~263)\n- Search indexing: `crates/comms_db_client/src/messages/get_channel_message.rs:6` `ChannelMessageInfo`; `crates/models_search/src/channel.rs:129`; `crates/opensearch_client/src/search/channels.rs:23`\n- Realtime websocket payload: `crates/channels/src/outbound/connection_gateway_realtime.rs:159` `MessageRealtimeData` (flattens `MutatedMessage` + `MessageRealtimeSender` at 166)\n\n## 2. How content is represented\n\n**Plain `String`.** Markdown text, rendered client-side. No content blocks, no enum of part types, no structured/rich parts anywhere in the channel path — every layer (`ChannelMessage`, `ThreadReply`, `ApiChannelMessage`, `MutatedMessage`, `TopLevelMessageRow`, soup, search, DB column) carries `content: String`.\n\nThe only structure adjacent to content:\n- Inline mention markup embedded *inside* the markdown string, extracted by the lexical service into `SimpleMention` rows (`crates/lexical_mention_extractor/src/lib.rs:27`, table `comms_entity_mentions`).\n- `MessageAttachment` / `comms_attachments` as a sibling list (entity_type/entity_id + width/height), not part of content.\n\nFrontend rendering: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/Content.tsx:14` — takes `message().content` and passes it whole to `StaticMarkdown` with `channelTheme`. `isEmojiOnly` bumps to big-emoji styling. That's the entire content rendering model.\n\n## 3. Non-human / bot / AI author — yes, this exists\n\n- `crates/channel_sender/src/lib.rs:18` — `ChannelSender<'a>(Either<BotIdStr, MacroUserIdStr>)`; `sender_id` in the DB is a namespaced principal string, parsed via `parse_from_str` (tries `BotIdStr` first, i.e. `bot|<uuid>`, else macro user id).\n- `crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs:25` — `BotSenderProfile { name: String, avatar_url: Option<String> }`\n- API discriminator: `crates/channels/src/inbound/axum_router.rs:1829-1853`\n```rust\npub struct ApiMessageSender {\n    #[serde(rename = \"type\")] sender_type: ApiMessageSenderType,\n    id: String,                      // bot uuid or user id, namespace stripped\n    name: Option<String>,            // bot display name\n    avatar_url: Option<String>,      // bot avatar\n    triggered_by: Option<String>,    // user who triggered the agent message\n}\npub enum ApiMessageSenderType { User, Bot }   // snake_case on the wire\n```\nbuilt by `ApiMessageSender::from_message_sender` (line 1893) — bot profile + `triggered_by` only attached when the sender is a bot.\n- `triggered_by` is set internally, never from the wire (`PostMessageRequest.triggered_by`, `#[serde(skip)]`).\n- Bot model: `crates/bots/src/domain/models.rs:104` `Bot { id: BotId, kind: BotKind, owner: Option<BotOwner>, name, handle, description, avatar_url, ... }`; `BotKind { Owned, System }` at line 14; `BotOwner { User{user_id}, Team{team_id} }` at line 87. Related crates: `crates/bot_id`, `crates/channel_bots`.\n- Frontend: `apps/web/src/lib/queries/channel/message-sender.ts` (`isBotSenderId`, `senderFromStorageId`, `normalizeChannelMessageSender`), `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/AgentBadge.tsx` (renders an \"Agent\" pill when `isBotSenderId(sender_id)`), `apps/web/src/features/channel/macroAi.ts` + `@core/constant/macroAgent` (the first-party Macro agent bot identity, `MACRO_AGENT_PRINCIPAL_ID` = `bot|<uuid>`).\n\n## 4. Message \"kind\"/\"type\" discriminator — none for content\n\nThe only `kind` that exists is **position**, not content type: `ChannelMessageKind { TopLevelMessage, ThreadReply }` at `crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs:104`, surfaced as `ApiChannelMessageKind` (`axum_router.rs:2198`) and `ToolMessageKind` (`toolset/types.rs:33`).\n\nThere is **no** system-message / join-leave / call-event variant on `comms_messages`. Non-plain-text UI is modeled *outside* the message stream:\n- Active call banner: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Channel/ActiveCallMessage.tsx` — a separate component driven by `useActiveCallQuery`, not a message row.\n- Channel-created marker: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/ChannelCreatedIndicator.tsx` — list decoration.\n- Date/new dividers: `DateDivider.tsx`, `NewDivider.tsx` — list decorations keyed off `ChannelMessageListMeta` (`Message/list-meta.ts`).\n- Deleted state: branch on `message.deleted_at != null` (`ChannelMessage.tsx:227` → `DeletedMessageLayout`).\n- Call transcripts fake a message: `apps/web/src/features/block-call/component/CallTranscript.tsx:79` `segmentToApiChannelMessage(...)` synthesizes an `ApiChannelMessage` from a transcript segment. Same trick for doc comments: `apps/web/src/lib/core/comments/discussion/Discussion.tsx:182` `discussionCommentToApiChannelMessage`.\n\nSo today the only way to render anything non-plain-text is to either synthesize a fake `ApiChannelMessage` or add a sibling component to the list.\n\n## 5. TypeScript types + renderer\n\n**Not specta.** utoipa → OpenAPI JSON → **orval** codegen.\n- Config: `apps/web/src/lib/service-clients/orval.config.ts` (channels live in the `document_storage_service` spec → `service-storage`).\n- Generated: `apps/web/src/lib/service-clients/service-storage/generated/schemas/apiChannelMessage.ts`, `apiMessageSender.ts`, `apiMessageSenderType.ts` (`{ user: 'user', bot: 'bot' }`), `apiThreadInfo.ts`, `apiThreadReply.ts`, `apiCountedReaction.ts`, `apiMessageAttachment.ts`, `apiChannelMessagesPage.ts`, `apiChannelMessageKind.ts`, plus `soupMessageSender*.ts`. Imported as `@service-storage/generated/schemas/...` or `@service-storage/client` (tsconfig path at `apps/web/tsconfig.json:92`).\n\n**Renderer:**\n- `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/ChannelMessage.tsx:198` — `ChannelMessage()`, the row component (Switch over deleted / grouped / regular layouts).\n- Compound namespace: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/Message.ts` — `Message.{Root, Layout, Slot, SenderName, AgentBadge, FromPill, SenderIcon, Timestamp, Content, Attachments, Reactions, EditedIndicator, HoverActions, ActionMenu, MediaPreview, ...}`\n- Frontend view model (deliberately looser than the API type): `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/types.ts` — `MessageData { id, content, sender_id, sender?: ApiMessageSender, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at?, edited_at?, thread_id?, attachments, reactions }`. This is what the whole Message tree consumes via `useMessage()` (`Message/context.ts`).\n- Consumers: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Thread/ChannelThread.tsx:308`, `Thread/ThreadReplyList.tsx:85`, `Channel/ThreadList.tsx` (virtua virtualizer), `apps/web/src/features/entity/composed/list-entity/channel.tsx:171`.\n- Queries/cache: `apps/web/src/lib/queries/channel/channel-messages.ts`, `reconcile.ts`, `message-sender.ts`.\n\n## 6. AI chat message model (for comparison)\n\n**Content parts enum — `crates/agent/src/types.rs`**\n- `Role` — line 32: `{ User, Assistant, System }` (lowercase)\n- `AssistantMessagePart` — **line 52**, `#[serde(tag = \"type\", rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`:\n```rust\npub enum AssistantMessagePart {\n    Text { text: String },\n    ToolCall { name: String, json: serde_json::Value, id: String },\n    McpToolCall { name: String, service: String, display_name: Option<String>, json: serde_json::Value, id: String },\n    ToolCallResponseJson { name: String, json: serde_json::Value, id: String },\n    ToolCallErr { name: String, description: String, id: String },\n    Thinking { thinking: String },\n}\n```\n- `ChatMessageContent` — **line 136**:\n```rust\n#[serde(untagged)]\npub enum ChatMessageContent {\n    Text(String),\n    AssistantMessageParts(Vec<AssistantMessagePart>),\n}\n```\nwith helpers `user_message_text`, `assistant_message_text`, `assistant_message_text_with_tools`, `message_text`, `message_text_with_tools` (lines 148–232). `ChatMessage { content, role, attachments }` at line 240; `ChatMessages(Vec<ChatMessage>)` at 255.\n\n**Persisted / API types — `crates/model/src/chat/message.rs`**\n- `ChatMessage` (line 10): `{ id: String, content: ChatMessageContent, role: Role, model: Option<String> }`, `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`, `sqlx::FromRow`\n- `ChatMessageWithAttachments` (line 23): same + `attachments: Vec<Entity<'static>>`\n- `NewChatMessage` (line 35)\n- DB: `public.\"ChatMessage\"` with **`content jsonb NOT NULL`** and `role text` — see `services/delete_chat_handler/migrations/20240325143515_basic_schema_for_testing.sql:343`\n- Chat crate: `crates/chat/src/domain/models/chat.rs:83` `ChatResponse { messages: Vec<ChatMessageWithAttachments>, ... }`; `crates/chat/src/domain/models/message.rs:8` `PatchChatMessageArgs { message_id, content: ChatMessageContent }`, `WebCitation` (line 17), `ResolvedMessageContent` (line 34); `crates/chat/src/domain/events.rs:104` `ChatMessageRole`.\n\n**Frontend AI renderer** (the analogue of `Message/Content.tsx`): `apps/web/src/lib/core/component/AI/component/message/AssistantMessageParts.tsx` — switches on `part.type` (`toolCall` / `mcpToolCall` / `toolCallErr` / `thinking` / `text`) into `RenderTool`, `McpToolCall`, `ThinkingBlock`, `ChatMessageMarkdown`, grouping tool activity into `AssistantActivityGroup`. Types come from `@service-cognition/generated/schemas/assistantMessagePart` (orval, cognition service spec).\n\n**Key contrast:** AI chat already has a tagged, extensible part enum persisted as jsonb with a per-part-type frontend renderer registry; channel messages are a flat `text` column with a single markdown renderer, and the only author/kind discriminators are `ApiMessageSenderType { user, bot }` (author) and `ChannelMessageKind { TopLevelMessage, ThreadReply }` (position). There is no content-kind discriminator on channel messages at all."),
                            },
                        ],
