                Text {
                    text: "Found them. Here's the picture.\n\n## Channel messages: flat text, no content structure\n\n`crates/channels/src/domain/models.rs:140` — `ChannelMessage` carries **`content: String`**. Same at every layer: `ApiChannelMessage` (`channels/src/inbound/axum_router.rs:1911`), `MutatedMessage`, the realtime websocket payload, soup/inbox (`models_soup/src/comms.rs:78`), search indexing, MCP toolset. The DB column is plain `text` (`macro_db_client/migrations/20251104101012_comms_db_schema.sql:93`) — no jsonb, no content-kind column.\n\nThere is **no content-kind discriminator at all**. The only `kind` is positional (`TopLevelMessage` / `ThreadReply`). Everything non-plain-text today is either a sibling component in the list (active call banner, dividers) or a **synthesized fake message** — `segmentToApiChannelMessage` for call transcripts, `discussionCommentToApiChannelMessage` for doc comments.\n\nRendering is one component: `apps/web/src/features/channel/Message/Content.tsx:14` → `StaticMarkdown`.\n\n## Bot authorship already exists — that part's done\n\n`crates/channel_sender/src/lib.rs:18` — `ChannelSender(Either<BotIdStr, MacroUserIdStr>)`, `sender_id` is a namespaced principal (`bot|<uuid>`). `ApiMessageSender { type: user|bot, id, name, avatar_url, triggered_by }`. Frontend already renders an \"Agent\" pill (`AgentBadge.tsx`). So *who* sent it is solved; only *what* it contains isn't.\n\n## AI content is already modeled — elsewhere\n\n`crates/agent/src/types.rs:52` — `AssistantMessagePart`, tagged enum: `Text | ToolCall | McpToolCall | ToolCallResponseJson | ToolCallErr | Thinking`, persisted as **jsonb** on `ChatMessage.content`, with a per-type frontend renderer registry at `AI/component/message/AssistantMessageParts.tsx`.\n\nSo the repo has two parallel worlds: AI chat has extensible jsonb parts + a renderer registry; channels have a text column + a markdown renderer.\n\n## Your input is a delta stream\n\nACP `SessionUpdate` (v1, `agent-client-protocol-schema`) is: `UserMessageChunk | AgentMessageChunk | AgentThoughtChunk | ToolCall | ToolCallUpdate | Plan | AvailableCommandsUpdate | CurrentModeUpdate | UsageUpdate`. That's genuinely a fold — chunks accumulate, `ToolCallUpdate` patches a prior `ToolCall` by id, `Plan` replaces.\n\nAnd the recordings are ideal fixtures — they're at `~/.agent_runtime_sessions/` (not `.agent_session_recordings/`), 3 sessions, direction-labelled ARP wire frames:\n```json\n{\"ts\":\"...\",\"direction\":\"to_server\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"acp_ready\"}}\n```\nThat's exactly `ToServerMessage`/`ToRuntimeMessage` JSON, so they replay straight through the fold.\n\n## The two decisions that gate everything\n\nNote ACP is richer than `AssistantMessagePart`: it has tool-call **status** (pending/in_progress/completed/failed), `ToolCallContent` with diffs and terminal output, plans, and permission requests. The DCS enum has none of that — it was shaped by Anthropic streaming, not ACP. My lean is a fresh vocabulary in `agent_fold` shaped after ACP, and an additive nullable `parts` column so every existing `content: String` consumer (search, soup, notifications, toolset) keeps working untouched.",
                },
