                Text {
                    text: "Now I have what I need. The recordings are the real spec here, and they surfaced four things that change the design:\n\n**1. Tool calls dominate.** 406 of ~450 ACP frames are `session/update`; within those, 175 `tool_call_update` vs 46 `tool_call` — ~4 patches per call. The fold is mostly a correlate-and-patch loop keyed on `toolCallId`, not a text accumulator.\n\n**2. `usage_update` is 81 frames of noise.** Nothing renderable. Drop, or aggregate once per turn.\n\n**3. The interesting data is in `_meta`, not in ACP.** ACP normalizes tools to a coarse `kind` (`execute`/`read`/`edit`). The actual tool name lives at `_meta.claudeCode.toolName` (`Bash`, `Write`, `Read`). Terminal output streams via `_meta.terminal_output` — **with raw ANSI escapes** — and the exit code via `_meta.terminal_exit`. None of that is standard ACP.\n\nSo a faithful fold **cannot be pure ACP**. It needs a harness-specific extension layer. I'd quarantine that explicitly rather than let `_meta` reads leak through the whole fold — one `ClaudeCodeMeta` extraction step, so a future harness slots in beside it instead of rewriting the core.\n\n**4. Frames arrive underspecified and get patched.** The `Write` tool call opens as `{\"rawInput\":{},\"status\":\"pending\",\"content\":[],\"locations\":[]}` — title is literally just `\"Write\"`. Everything useful arrives later. And `session/request_permission` is a request/response pair correlated by JSON-RPC **id**, not `toolCallId` — a pending permission is a renderable state that later resolves.\n\n## Proposed vocabulary\n\n```rust\n/// One renderable message. Derived, never stored.\npub struct AgentMessage {\n    pub turn: TurnId,                          // prompt → stopReason\n    pub parts: NonEmpty<AgentMessagePart>,\n}\n\npub enum AgentMessagePart {\n    Text(Markdown),\n    Thought(Markdown),\n    ToolUse(ToolUse),\n    Permission(PermissionPrompt),              // pending | resolved(outcome)\n}\n\npub struct ToolUse {\n    pub id: ToolUseId,                         // ACP toolCallId\n    pub label: String,                         // _meta tool name, else title\n    pub status: ToolStatus,                    // Pending | Running | Completed | Failed\n    pub detail: ToolDetail,\n}\n\npub enum ToolDetail {\n    Terminal { command: String, output: AnsiText, exit_code: Option<i32> },\n    FileEdit { path: PathBuf, diff: Option<Diff> },\n    FileRead { path: PathBuf },\n    Other  { kind: String, input: serde_json::Value },\n}\n```\n\n`AnsiText` as its own type because that decision has to land somewhere — strip at fold time or preserve and render client-side. I'd preserve; stripping is lossy and the frontend can decide.\n\n## Two consequences for what you stubbed\n\n**The fold is pure and infallible.** The log's `content` jsonb is already deserialized into `agent_session::domain::model::Message` by the repo (`crates/agent_session/src/domain/model.rs:60`), so the fold's input is typed on arrival. Unknown/irrelevant frames are skipped, not errored. That makes `domain/error.rs` dead — signature is just:\n\n```rust\nfn fold(log: impl IntoIterator<Item = AgentSessionLog>) -> Vec<AgentMessage>\n```\n\n**There's no port to define.** A pure fold does no I/O; the log source is already `agent_session`'s repo. So `agent_fold` wants to be a plain library with a free function and a `test.rs` replaying those three `.jsonl` files — not a hex crate with `domain/ports.rs`. Your trait stub is probably worth deleting rather than filling in.\n\nOne thing I'd want your call on before writing types: **granularity within a turn.** One `AgentMessage` per turn with parts in order (frontend collapses runs of `ToolUse` into an activity group) reads best as a channel message and is what I'd default to — but it means a turn is one big message that grows. The alternative is splitting a new message each time text follows tool activity, which gives a more conversational channel feel at the cost of a fuzzier boundary rule.Empirically answerable — let me check whether the log actually produces orphans.",
                },
                ToolUse {
                    id: ToolUseId(
                        "toolu_01AYc17jWRchH926P73NPt6L",
                    ),
                    label: "Bash",
                    status: Completed,
                    detail: Terminal {
                        command: Some(
                            "cd ~/.agent_runtime_sessions && for f in *.jsonl; do echo \"=== $f\"; \nopened=$(jq -r 'select(.content.params.update.sessionUpdate==\"tool_call\") | .content.params.update.toolCallId' $f | sort -u)\nupdated=$(jq -r 'select(.content.params.update.sessionUpdate==\"tool_call_update\") | .content.params.update.toolCallId' $f | sort -u)\necho \"opened=$(echo \"$opened\" | grep -c . )  updated=$(echo \"$updated\" | grep -c .)\"\necho \"orphan updates (patch w/ no open):\"; comm -13 <(echo \"$opened\") <(echo \"$updated\") | sed 's/^/    /'\necho \"never reached terminal status:\"\nfor id in $opened; do\n  last=$(jq -r \"select(.content.params.update.toolCallId==\\\"$id\\\") | .content.params.update.status // empty\" $f | tail -1)\n  case \"$last\" in completed|failed) ;; *) echo \"    $id last_status=${last:-none}\";; esac\ndone\ndone",
                        ),
                        output: Some(
                            AnsiText(
                                "=== 1c6f5dbc-0fa8-4558-8ebb-3165a1daea56.jsonl\nopened=30  updated=29\norphan updates (patch w/ no open):\nnever reached terminal status:\n    toolu_011jsLuU3pdvMBZ5UQuv87Mz\ntoolu_01352etHpBLWV1h8TL9UTmdc\ntoolu_013ZZhkrMVi1WUobYm5iLFBp\ntoolu_014E1teRuKvFVz3kXjjkS9Ah\ntoolu_015cPCzRzsgaeC5T4RKwfcqt\ntoolu_0166v7nKJaZsGG5TUqPcomaa\ntoolu_017CKQR5Ypi2BbXyyEWi9epq\ntoolu_018ArD4ZmaWuxEXW1KVfWxWi\ntoolu_018WB6FehVLcrszUvj598DeC\ntoolu_018xbq9fhqGHb88EBgsfVisi\ntoolu_019NXxCRZdm2cgJ4haDXmfRn\ntoolu_019iCEBqeqsXYMJQdJhvGZzE\ntoolu_01ATR61Vo1sUBC4sDTb9hgkQ\ntoolu_01B21mvnKULwrxijSpbU4hgU\ntoolu_01BSkUBhuv3VSJMmEXidfKDZ\ntoolu_01Ex1sHJeme9xM23T9tuUtvW\ntoolu_01F5V288iQ8iArGM4B3ayCFm\ntoolu_01FMZq9Myj3VrRZScNV2vx4o\ntoolu_01HocEetuSapsmVgT3isZYfw\ntoolu_01JnxGKMHWwnZCHCc7RWuBxk\ntoolu_01LPjM3sh7fjLME6aNNvbYtu\ntoolu_01MRKTuvyiKzhsv37MTRfvmQ\ntoolu_01MohDMjaUKCtkLJXFwjMqVY\ntoolu_01NuY6RvJBEwhYApLPbV3QfA\ntoolu_01T6GAjr5YEZpBifkp3vj1N9\ntoolu_01ULC7SdcZW6QpLwibk2SdF9\ntoolu_01V4uph7ZkZKaPpgF6UE4Nop\ntoolu_01VdTdh7sXMuLbz5B7D35poo\ntoolu_01XiuBq9trG9cXnZA3wDu7Gp\ntoolu_01Y6KvTMTESF9qJwnVDWLMMh last_status=none\n=== ab25cf29-d876-4ec6-9c30-dac24f13bcfe.jsonl\nopened=0  updated=0\norphan updates (patch w/ no open):\nnever reached terminal status:\n=== cdf15e0e-c8b7-486e-93de-f596f547e641.jsonl\nopened=16  updated=16\norphan updates (patch w/ no open):\nnever reached terminal status:\n    toolu_011EjWXxbBUL3LeeWdhwZzVE\ntoolu_014z9EgjHhbpdT4oiKKbKVoi\ntoolu_015c1NGtLCDbzzN6gLsNek6c\ntoolu_017vXvd3YJFsTDHjuqH1pm9J\ntoolu_01C3WXuHqyYExW1fkiSdhQBm\ntoolu_01C7ZWnHKJy4TwzpXiReZgcz\ntoolu_01CtXAUSJxvsbs2FD7QmMqDu\ntoolu_01ETt3DxUVQNopgU44xbSc69\ntoolu_01GSaPYdcfh8YP2kDfjgb3v9\ntoolu_01JmdVCbwRjVNdCaXZAy6rL8\ntoolu_01JzF7TRdp8Hua7s8ogcF8bK\ntoolu_01KsnUYkdiXpsCnKiLAaBwEC\ntoolu_01RDnLaxGffMSSDvnHToEarF\ntoolu_01SfjW3NaG4UD6znQMU23cyf\ntoolu_01V3ua93NVQMzvw1UuSyz5Ds\ntoolu_01VScDhwjTxikVfbmwUoxaok last_status=none\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/eric/Cod