                    ),
                },
                Text {
                    text: "Restructured into a hex crate with the pretend-DB made explicit. **Hexagonal boundary checked** (via the architecture skill): domain imports only other domain models (`agent_session::domain::model`), protocol schema, and `tracing` — no axum/sqlx/transport anywhere; the one adapter lives in `outbound/`. There's no authz or business policy in this crate yet — queries are scoped by `AgentSessionId`, and access control (who may read a session's messages) stays with whatever inbound surface eventually calls the repo, minting its receipt against the session's thread/channel.\n\n**The shape now:**\n\n```\nsrc/domain/\n  message.rs   FoldedMessage vocabulary + MessageId natural key (turn, AuthorKind)\n  fold.rs      the pure total fold — unchanged semantics, now eats AgentSessionLog directly\n  meta.rs      quarantined Claude-Code _meta readers\n  ports.rs     SessionLogStore (driven) · FoldedMessageRepo (driving)\n  service.rs   FoldedMessageService: folds on every read, warns anomalies\nsrc/outbound/\n  memory.rs    InMemoryLogStore — what make-believe runs on\n```\n\n**Key decisions in the restructure:**\n- **The duplication went away.** My `LogEntry`/`LogMessage` were `agent_session::domain::model::{AgentSessionLog, Message}` re-invented — the fold now consumes the real model, so the eventual Postgres adapter is `AgentSessionLogRepo::list_by_session` output passed straight through.\n- **`FoldedMessageRepo` is the fiction.** Repo-shaped API (`list_by_session`, `get(session, id)`), styled after the channels crate: RPITIT `+ Send`, `rootcause::Report`, `#[tracing::instrument(err, skip(self))]`. Callers can't tell nothing is stored; if messages ever materialize, only the implementation moves.\n- **Messages got a natural key.** No rows means no surrogate ids, but the fold's shape gives one for free: `(turn, author side)` — deterministic across re-derivation, so `get` and future streaming reconciliation have something stable to address.\n- **Anomalies stay out of the query API.** A DB read doesn't fail because one row is odd — the service `tracing::warn!`s them; tests still assert-empty via the bare fold.\n- **Deferred:** the real Postgres adapter (belongs at the composition root — a generic wrapper over `AgentSessionLogRepo` can't prove `Send` since that trait doesn't bound its futures) and the `inbound/` comms adapter, per your earlier hold-off.\n\n12 tests + doctest green (fold suite, new service suite covering session scoping / get-by-id / service≡fold equivalence, recordings replay), strict clippy (`-Dwarnings`) clean, and `fold_recording` now exercises the full hexagon: recording → `InMemoryLogStore` → service → rendered turns.Two clear changes. Let me check what I need for both.",
                },
