                    label: "Bash",
                    status: Completed,
                    detail: Terminal {
                        command: Some(
                            "cat > /tmp/mem_fold.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: project-agent-fold\ndescription: agent_fold crate — hex crate folding agent_session_log ACP frames into messages queried as if stored; comms rendering in inbound\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`crates/agent_fold` (started 2026-08-03) folds the `agent_session_log` protocol log (ARP v0 frames wrapping ACP) into renderable messages. Related: [[project-agent-container-integration]].\n\nDesign decisions (Eric's calls, in order given):\n- **Parallel system** — ignore existing AI chat models (`AssistantMessagePart` etc.); nothing persisted, derived on every read (\"type land\")\n- **No Result on the fold** — total by construction; renderable-partial beats failing (pending tool call = in-flight state, not error). Weirdness → `Fold::anomalies` (tests assert empty; prod degrades gracefully). A fold error would mean a blank channel.\n- **One explicit match**, not a handler registry — every understood/ignored frame named in one place\n- **Hex crate with a pretend DB** — reversed an earlier plain-lib decision. Messages queried *as if stored*: `FoldedMessageRepo` (list_by_session / get by natural key `MessageId{turn, AuthorKind}`), `FoldedMessageService` folds on read, anomalies → `tracing::warn`\n- **Domain names no display type** — comms coupling lives only in `inbound/comms_message.rs` (Eric: \"beautiful / abstract way that doesn't inject / depend on comms messages at all in the domain\")\n- **Reuse agent_session's log store** — no duplicate `SessionLogStore` port, no `outbound/` module; expand agent_session instead (added `+ Send` to both port traits + `testing::InMemoryAgentSessionRepo` behind `test-utils`)\n\nLayout: `domain/{message,fold,meta,ports,service,test_support}.rs`, `inbound/comms_message.rs`. Ports follow channels style: RPITIT `+ Send`, `rootcause::Report`, `#[tracing::instrument(err, skip(self))]`.\n\n`inbound/comms_message.rs`: renders `FoldedMessage` → `channels::domain::models::ChannelMessage`. **Lossy on purpose** — `content` is a `String` today so parts flatten to markdown (tool calls → fenced blocks w/ status markers ●◦◍✕, thoughts → blockquote, ANSI stripped here since domain preserves it). Swap `render_markdown` when comms carries structured parts. `CommsContext` comes off the `AgentSession` record itself (it already has `thread_id` + `bot_id`). Message ids = UUIDv5 from (session, turn, author) so re-reads are stable — otherwise every poll looks like new messages.\n\nEmpirics from recordings (`~/.agent_runtime_sessions/*.jsonl`, NOT .agent_session_recordings): ~4 tool_call_update per tool_call; usage_update is noise (81/450 frames); tool opens arrive underspecified (`Write` opens with empty rawInput); real tool name + terminal output ONLY in `_meta` (ACP normalizes to coarse `kind`) — hence quarantined `domain/meta.rs`; log order sound (uuid v7 + created_at tiebreak) so orphan patches need a `session/load` resume.\n\nIterate: `cargo run -p agent_fold --example fold_recording -- <recording.jsonl>` prints domain messages AND channel-message markdown. Test `replays_local_recordings` folds all local recordings asserting zero anomalies (no-op in CI where dir absent).\n\nKnown gaps: `AgentSessionLog` carries no `created_at`, so rendered timestamps are epoch (thread a frame timestamp through the model to fix); `SessionUpdate::Plan` deliberately unmodelled → anomaly until a recording produces one; no inbound axum router yet; no authz (queries scoped by AgentSessionId only).\nEOF\ncp /tmp/mem_fold.md /Users/eric/.claude/projects/-Users-eric-Code-macro/memory/project_agent_fold.md && echo written",
